        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "What is the value of  $\\frac{2}{25}\\int_{10}^{20}\\frac{3{log}_{2}({\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)}^{2})}{\\sqrt{2}\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=\\log_{2}\\left(\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)^{2}\\right).$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{x \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}\\,\u27f9\\,\\frac{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{2}\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $10$ | $20$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{25}\\int_{10}^{20}\\frac{3{log}_{2}({\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)}^{2})}{\\sqrt{2}\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{25}\\int_{10}^{20}{log}_{2}({\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{5}\\int_{2}^{4}u\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}2}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{3 \\sqrt{2} \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{10}\\int_{2}^{4}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}2}{2\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}\\right)|_{2}^{4} \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}2}{4\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot (16-4)\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{9\\operatorname{ln}2}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
